30. June 2021Explanation: This example demonstrates different ways to format a date. It uses predefined patterns, locale-specific formatting, and a custom formatter built using DateTimeFormatterBuilder to display the date in different formats.Common Methods of DateTimeFormatterBuilderThey are pictorially depicted below in tabular format in alphabetical alongside the action performed by them which are as follows:MethodDescriptionappend(DateTimeFormatter formatter)Appends the elements of another formatter to the builder.appendPattern(String pattern)Appends date-time elements defined by a pattern.appendLiteral(char literal)Appends a character literal to the formatter.appendLiteral(String literal)Appends a string literal to the formatter.appendValue(TemporalField field)Appends the numeric value of the specified date-time field.appendText(TemporalField field)Appends the textual representation of a date-time field.appendFraction(TemporalField field, int minWidth, int maxWidth, boolean decimalPoint)Appends the fractional value of a date-time field.appendOptional(DateTimeFormatter formatter)Appends another formatter as an optional section.optionalStart()Marks the beginning of an optional section.optionalEnd()Marks the end of an optional section.parseCaseInsensitive()Makes subsequent parsing case-insensitive.parseCaseSensitive()Makes subsequent parsing case-sensitive.parseDefaulting(TemporalField field, long value)Provides a default value for a field when it is absent during parsing.toFormatter()Creates a DateTimeFormatter from the builder using the default locale.toFormatter(Locale locale)Creates a DateTimeFormatter using the specified locale.Advantages of DateTimeFormatterBuilderComplex Formatting: Builds formatters that go beyond simple pattern-based formatting.Flexible Parsing: Supports optional sections and default values for handling different input formats.Custom Formatting Rules: Allows literals, fields, text styles, and other formatting components to be combined as required.Reusable Formatters: The resulting DateTimeFormatter objects can be reused for formatting and parsing.
